  "description": "config.v1 §2.15: what the view, the status, the change event, an error envelope and a log line may carry for a sensitive value. A case gives one group as the view declares it, the owner's running values before the change ({parameter: {value, source}}), the startup values ({parameter: value}: what a restart would give), a SetRequest on the group, and device_words, what the device would say refusing it (or null). The owner applies the request's values (source runtime; a dry run applies nothing, and is shown as its would-be view). expect.view is the group's parameters as the view then shows them (§2.3: startup only where it differs from a known running value, and never for a sensitive parameter); expect.status the group's member of the status's values, or null when the status leaves the group out; expect.edits the change event's edits, or null when there is no event (a dry run); expect.log the request as the owner logs it, each sensitive value written \"<redacted>\"; expect.device_detail the ConfigError detail of a device-refused envelope given device_words, null when the words are left out or there are none. A request the owner refuses instead expects {refused: {code, field, message_repeats_value}}, as validation.json reads code and field; message_repeats_value says whether the envelope's message contains the refused value, as its JSON text or, for a string, the string itself, which it never does."
